WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Guys, tonight was the big
Rockefeller Center

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:02.736 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Christmas tree lighting.

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:05.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you see it?
Well, yeah.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.873 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were thousands of people
out in the plaza.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:11.111
It was really nice
watching parents show their kids

00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:13.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
the true meaning
of claustrophobia.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.616 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:19.152
The tree lighting is such
a great tradition, though.

00:00:19.152 --> 00:00:21.087
It's fun for everyone --
except the guy who waited

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.022 line:92%
four hours in the freezing cold,

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
then sneezed
and totally missed it.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.058 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It's like, "Ah-choo!"

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, you're kidding me!
You're joking me!"

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:28.528 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the tree is beautiful.
It's so pretty.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
You barely notice the 80-foot
orange extension cord

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
running from the star
to the bottom.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:36.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
You barely --
You can barely see it.

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's cute.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
Actually, I read that
the star weighs 900 pounds

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
and features
3 million crystals.

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:43.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
900 pounds
and 3 million crystals,

00:00:45.512 --> 00:00:48.048
or as guys from New Jersey call
that a pinky ring.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, whoa."
-"Oh!"

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Hey, yo."
-"Hey!"

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"We gonna
light this tree over here?

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why don't you
light it right now.

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
Turn the tree on.
No one has to know."

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.393 line:92%
Oh, I saw that tonight was also

00:01:00.393 --> 00:01:03.997
the Christmas-tree-lighting
ceremony at the White House.

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.465 size:75% position:38%
President Trump said
it's the only time

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.467
he can press a giant button
without everyone in America

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.203
being absolutely terrified.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
"3, 2 --
Ooh! Gotcha!"

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:15.575 line:92%
Why would you do it on two?

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.813 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Who does that?

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:20.480 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This is interesting.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you wanted to go
to the White House ceremony,

00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:25.218
you can get free tickets
through an online lottery.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:25.752 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:28.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody did,
but you could have done it.

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.325 size:81% position:41%
-You gotta know how --
-Who does it on two?

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Why would you do it?
Yeah.

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everyone's waiting for one.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:01:34.561 --> 00:01:37.330
-Everybody's gonna cheer on one,
but let's do --

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
No. Why?
-"I'm in charge."

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.535 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-"I go with my gut."

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.636 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.636 --> 00:01:45.171 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Doesn't make any sense.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.172 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, the White House
and 30 Rock

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
had their tree-lighting
ceremonies on the same night.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
In many ways,
the events are similar,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there are
some key differences.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.112 line:92%
I'll show you what I mean.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.814
First, at 30 Rock, everyone
gathers to see the tree get lit.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.884
At the White House, everyone
who works for Trump gets lit.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:05.992 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:05.992 --> 00:02:09.929
Next at 30 Rock, music superstar
John Legend sings the hits.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.663 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And at the White House,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
Commerce Secretary Wilbur Ross
plays the spoons.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.307 size:75% position:38% line:92%
♪♪ Camptown races ♪♪

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:23.610 size:75% position:38%
-Finally at 30 Rock,
the tree is donated

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
to Habitat for Humanity
to build homes.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.982
At the White House, the tree
is chopped up to build the wall.

00:02:28.982 --> 00:02:29.682 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:32.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The wall."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:35.989
Well, tomorrow, Trump heads
to Argentina for the G20 summit,

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
where world leaders
are hoping to issue

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.692 size:78% position:39%
some joint statements
on climate change.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump actually
co-wrote statements

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
with several other leaders,
though I'm not sure

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
he had all of
his facts straight.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
Check out some of these
joint statements.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
British Prime Minister
Theresa May wrote,

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:51.804
"The reason so many ecosystems
are disappearing is because..."

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.773 line:92%
and Trump wrote, "I fired them."

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.975 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
German Chancellor
Angela Merkel wrote,

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
"We can conserve
our available water if..."

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump wrote,
"...we drink it with two hands

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.083 size:84% position:42% line:92%
as slowly as possible."

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.619 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.189 size:84% position:42%
Canadian Prime Minister
Justin Trudeau wrote,

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.456 line:92%
"The only thing more concerning

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:12.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
than the fallout
of El Niño is..."

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump wrote, "...the fallout
of el baño.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
I wouldn't go in there
if I were you."

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.197 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
What?
-Why would he --

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why would he release that
statement?

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.969
-And finally, Japanese
Prime Minister Shinzo Abe wrote,

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:26.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Reduce, reuse..."
and Trump wrote, "...retweet!"

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.374 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're not on the same page.
-No, not at all.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.280 line:92%
-Some more political news.

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
I saw that Ohio Senator
Sherrod Brown

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.551 size:88% position:44%
is seriously considering
running for president.

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it turns out
he's not the only one.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
Check out what these
other Senators had to say

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
when asked
if they thought about running.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:46.226
First, Senator Todd Young said,
"I thought about running,

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:49.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think I might be, too,
well, my last name."

00:03:49.696 --> 00:03:50.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then Senator Jeff Flake said,
"I thought about running,

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:54.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
but to be honest,
I'd probably drop out

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the last second,
and, well, my last name."

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:58.137 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Senator Angus King said,
"I thought about running,

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I don't really want
to be a president.

00:04:02.742 --> 00:04:05.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd rather be a,
well, my last name."

00:04:05.011 --> 00:04:05.545 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.614
And finally,
Senator Sheldon Whitehouse said,

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:08.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Of course
I thought about running,

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:10.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
but where would I live,
you idiot?"

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.253 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:14.954 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's so rude.
-Little harsh!

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:16.689 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, guys,
did you guys see this?

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a massive cow
in Australia.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:21.327 line:92%
Have you seen photos of this?

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Have you not seen this yet?

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.531 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a giant cow
or something like that.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.099 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's going viral.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's in Australia,
and people can't --

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look at this thing.
Check this out.

00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:32.272
-A cow Down Under has risen
to international stardom.

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:35.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The steer is named Knickers.
Kind of a big guy.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:35.775 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:37.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
He weighs more than
3,000 pounds.

00:04:37.944 --> 00:04:40.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Holy!
-More than 6 feet tall.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow!
-Wow!

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:44.484 line:92%
-That's the only cow on Earth

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.186 size:84% position:42%
who goes up to a farmer
and says, "Milk me!"

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:53.026 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:55.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Listen to this, guys.
I heard that Prince Harry

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:58.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
feels imprisoned
living in a royal palace.

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.867
To be fair,
you wouldn't feel great, either,

00:05:00.867 --> 00:05:01.634 size:88% position:44% line:92%
if you were 34 years old

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
and still crashing
at your grandma's.

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.304 --> 00:05:05.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
Guys, I'm very excited
about this.

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.373 size:84% position:42%
We have Macaulay Culkin
on the show tonight.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes!

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.715 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Macaulay Culkin.

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:17.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this time,
he's actually supposed to be

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:19.686 line:92%
in New York during the holidays.

00:05:19.686 --> 00:05:21.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:22.889 line:92%
Also, from "Law &amp; Order: SVU,"

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
Ice T and Mariska Hargitay
are here!

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.399 size:75% position:38%
It's actually weird.
Earlier, I went to

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:37.637
the dressing room to say hi,
but they had gone missing.

00:05:37.637 --> 00:05:39.572 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:41.607 size:78% position:39%
And, finally, I read,
earlier this month,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
a mysterious rumble
shook the Earth,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
but experts don't know
what caused it.

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
Though I'm pretty sure
it was just

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
that giant cow whispering,
"Moo!"

00:05:48.648 --> 00:05:52.418 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have a great show tonight.
Give it up for The Roots!

